# SEO / GEO (Site Machinery NZ)

Priority when auditing or changing the public site: **0 → 1 → 3 → 2 → 4 → 5–8**.

## 0. Crawler access
- `public/robots.txt` must **Allow** GPTBot, OAI-SearchBot, ChatGPT-User, Google-Extended, ClaudeBot, PerplexityBot, Perplexity-User, Applebot-Extended (not only `User-agent: *`).
- Host is GitHub Pages (no Cloudflare bot fight by default). If a CDN/WAF is added later, check dashboard bot rules separately.
- Do not gate indexable copy behind login, paywalls, or click-only UI.

## 1. Rendering & indexing
- Build must prerender crawlable HTML into `#root` (`scripts/prerender-meta.mjs` + `src/data/staticPages.js`). Homepage needs a static **`<h1>`** (hero), not JS-only.
- Every indexable route: HTTPS canonical (`src/data/seo.js`), sitemap entry, `robots.txt` Sitemap line.
- Run `npm run build` (includes `assert-seo.mjs`) before claiming SEO done.

## 2. llms.txt
- Maintain hand-written `public/llms.txt` (brand one-liner + key page links). Never ship a generic host auto-file.

## 3. Structured data
- Home: LocalBusiness + Organization, WebSite, SoftwareApplication (profit calculator) via `@graph`.
- Products: Product; `/for/*`: Service + areaServed; mesh guide: HowTo + SoftwareApplication.
- Schema must be in the static build, not client-only injection.

## 4. Content
- Prefer proprietary NZ data, first-party tools/charts, case notes, or distinct expert takes — cut generic how-to rehashes.
- Lead sections with a standalone 1–2 sentence answer; clear H1→H2→H3; tables/lists over long prose.

## 5–8. Operator (not always in-repo)
- Align Google Business Profile to NAP/services on the site (`docs/SEO-FOLLOW-UPS.md`).
- Off-site: consistent **Site Machinery NZ** naming; YouTube/email as non-search channels.
- Measure AI citations manually (ChatGPT/Perplexity/Gemini/Claude prompts) — Search Console will not show them.

Source of truth: `src/data/seo.js`, `public/robots.txt`, `public/llms.txt`, `docs/SEO-FOLLOW-UPS.md`.
